    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d6">

                <pb facs="0022" n="10" xml:id="pg10"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">856.48/3–545: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in the United
                        Kingdom</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Winant</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-03-12T22:00:00-04:00">March 12, 1945—10
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1904. Department received following <hi rendition="#italic">aide-mémoire</hi>
                    from Netherlands Embassy dated March 5:</p>
                <p>[Here follows text of <hi rendition="#italic">aide-mémoire</hi> printed <hi
                        rendition="#italic">supra</hi>.]</p>
                <p>This proposal raises questions relative both to blockade and British supply
                    situation and stockpiles. Before considering proposal further or taking it up
                    with military here Department would appreciate your ascertaining how far British
                    have gone with Netherlands in approving proposal on blockade grounds and in
                    agreeing on supply grounds. The latter point involves problem of British
                    stockpiles and their replenishment, which will be handled separately and you
                    should not enter into discussions with British on that matter. Has EWD<anchor
                        n="7" xml:id="d6-f1"/> any information as to attitude of SHAEF on blockade
                    aspect of introduction of proposed supplies into Netherlands or whether
                    Netherlands authorities have raised this question with SHAEF.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stettinius</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d6-f1" n="7" xml:id="d6-f1-content">
                <p>Economic Warfare Division of the Embassy in London.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
